  "name": "shuteye",
  "description": "A minimalist Rust library providing high-resolution nanosecond sleep functionality by wrapping platform-specific POSIX syscalls. It abstracts `clock_nanosleep` on Linux and `nanosleep` on macOS through a unified FFI interface and a `Timespec` utility struct. The crate is designed for systems programming tasks requiring precise, low-latency thread suspension with support for monotonic clock references.",
